{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778562021013,"sessionID":"ses_1e575b859ffeaH7zw4RGyzLU2h","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8793c1a056f57078","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"serous demilune cell"},"output":"Found 4 matches\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json:\n  Line 2:   \"body\": \"Links: #3471 \\n\\nPlease check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nserous demilune cell of salivary gland\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nserous demilune cell — Source: Amano et al. (2012), PMID:23209333 (exact synonym)\\ndemilune cell of salivary gland — Source: Amano et al. (2012) (related synonym)\\nserous crescent cell — Source: standard histology nomenclature (related synonym)\\nCrescents of Giannuzzi https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serous_demilune\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nA serous secreting cell that is part of a salivary gland, forming crescent-shaped (demilune) caps at the distal ends of mucous acini in mixed glands. Prominent in human submandibular and sublingual glands, this cell delivers its watery, enzyme-rich secretions — including α-amylase — through intercellular canaliculi that run between adjacent mucous cells to reach the acinar lumen (Amano et al., 2012). In rodents, these cells also express neuronal nitric oxide synthase (nNOS) (Isola, 2026).\\\"\\n\\nPMID:23209333\\nPMID:41686279\\n\\ncomment:\\nThe classic crescent-shaped morphology that gives demilune cells their name is a well-established histological feature, but must be caveated with the fixation artifact issue raised by Yamashina and others. Amano et al. (2012) describe how rapid-freeze fixation reveals a more tubular arrangement, suggesting the demilune shape is at least partly artifactual.\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\nCL:0000313\\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\n0000-0002-5507-2103\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\npart_of saliva-secreting gland (UBERON:0001044) — Source: Amano et al., 2012\\ncapable_of par...\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 35940: # Class: obo:CL_9900001 (serous demilune cell of salivary gland)\n\n  Line 35946: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23209333\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_9900001 \"serous demilune cell\")\n\n  Line 35951: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_9900001 \"serous demilune cell of salivary gland\")\n","metadata":{"matches":4,"truncated":false},"title":"serous demilune cell","time":{"start":1778562020971,"end":1778562021012}},"id":"prt_e1a8eacc9001iAPchSlYAzfJGx","sessionID":"ses_1e575b859ffeaH7zw4RGyzLU2h","messageID":"msg_e1a8aba29001zkjLMhRVPLPqUl"}}
